build*/

# libFuzzer writes its artifacts as crash-<sha1>, leak-<sha1>, timeout-<sha1>, oom-<sha1>
# and slow-unit-<sha1> into the artifact_prefix directory, which defaults to wherever the
# fuzzer was run. Nothing a campaign produces from this target may be committed — those
# bytes are derived from target content, and this repository will not always be private.
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*
slow-unit-*

# The one exception, by exact path. `crash-literal-tab.bin` is the authored reproducer for
# the seeded defect: we wrote it, it was reviewed, and P0-8 requires the reproducer to
# replay from a clean checkout — so a clone that silently lacks it produces a mission that
# cannot demonstrate anything.
#
# It needs naming explicitly because it collides with the `crash-*` rule above, which is
# exactly the generated-artifact pattern. Nothing distinguishes an authored fixture from a
# generated one but this line.
#
# `git check-ignore` without `--no-index` will NOT show this file as ignored once it is
# tracked, which is how the collision survived review in the first place. The assertion
# that matters is in tests/architecture/test_fuzz_artifacts_are_ignored.py, which asks
# whether a *fresh clone* would ignore it.
!crash/
!crash/crash-literal-tab.bin
